WEBVTT

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.300
If a task stops,

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.630
read the message before

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:03.650
changing settings.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.250
Open the Queue

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.880
and find the affected vehicle.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:08.940
Failed means there's

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:09.980
a message to check.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:11.670
Processing means

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.050
the job is still working.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:14.730
Give that job time

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.410
instead of adding it again.

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:18.930
If Facebook needs to reconnect,

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.690
start in the left sidebar.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:22.730
Click Configuration.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.760
Open the Facebook tab,

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.720
then choose Reconnect Facebook.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.470
Complete the sign-in

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.490
steps privately.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.540
Back in AutoLander,

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:32.660
check Facebook Connected

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:33.680
at the top right.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.660
Review the affected job

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.480
before retrying it, and leave

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.080
successful vehicles alone.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.900
If vehicles are missing, first

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.500
clear the search and filters

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.660
in Post to Market.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:46.250
Still missing?

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.700
Click Configuration

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:48.820
in the left sidebar.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.050
Choose Inventory Feeds

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.530
and check the connected source.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:53.880
Make sure it's

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:54.900
the right dealership

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.070
before changing anything.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:58.170
For Auto-Pilot, check

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.040
four things: is it on,

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.610
is it within the posting

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:03.610
window, is the computer online,

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.850
and is AutoLander running?

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:07.400
Read any

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.420
warning on the screen.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.240
If you still need help,

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.620
record what you tried,

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:12.880
what you expected

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:14.400
and the exact message.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:15.840
Add the time

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.090
and a screenshot without

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:18.110
private information.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.180
To find the app version,

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:21.280
click Configuration,

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:22.560
then Updates.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.680
On a dealer account, send

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.160
those details to your manager.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.960
On an individual account,

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.860
contact the AutoLander admin

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.760
through Support in the sidebar.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.940
Use the workbook's help form

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.340
to practice writing a clear

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:36.520
report for this example.
